{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_the_engineering_calculation_workspace", "label": "The Engineering Calculation Workspace", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_d_028", "label": "D-028", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TempestOS v1 is a client project system of record that evidence is tagged to; nothing new computes in Tempest in v1.0. Surfaces kept in place rather than stripped because pivoting later is cheaper than rebuilding."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_bracketcalculationworkbench", "label": "BracketCalculationWorkbench", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Composes four governed acts it does not own and formats every value with its unit before the Desktop sees it: no second engine, no duplicated arithmetic, no business logic in the Desktop layer."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_engineeringcalculationregister", "label": "EngineeringCalculationRegister", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gives each executed calculation the governed Calculation object the platform already had, linked through the existing calculatedBy relationship; nothing new invented."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_engineeringcalculationview", "label": "EngineeringCalculationView", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_engineeringcalculationcoordinator", "label": "EngineeringCalculationCoordinator", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_productcalculationcatalogue_registerall", "label": "ProductCalculationCatalogue.RegisterAll", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs from TempestHost before the first module initialises, not a discipline composition root, because a module may legitimately calculate while still initialising; the guard starts a host with no modules loaded."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_registered_for_the_test_not_for_the_user", "label": "Registered for the Test Not for the User", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A definition registered only where a sample or test assembly registers it passes every test and fails every user, because the test process dependency graph is not the production host."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_calculations_recordindex", "label": "Calculations.RecordIndex", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same IPersistenceStore index convention every reference catalogue uses; ListRecordsAsync returns summaries because a mixed list needs each entry type."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_adr_0143", "label": "ADR-0143", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A calculation carries the ReferencePin of the material revision it stood on inside its result; refuses a generic property resolver, a CalculationBase hierarchy, a second persistence mechanism and automatic approval."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_governedbracketcheckservice", "label": "GovernedBracketCheckService", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_bracketsectioncheckresult", "label": "BracketSectionCheckResult", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_icalculationengine_findrecordasync", "label": "ICalculationEngine.FindRecordAsync", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_retirement_is_not_delete", "label": "Retirement Is Not Delete", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "IDeletable.DeleteAsync is a one-way door that makes traceable work vanish; retirement moves to the nearest terminal state Cancelled, since no Draft to Archived transition exists (TD-169, a board decision)."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_guard_disarmed_by_every_path", "label": "Guard Disarmed by Every Path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A guard cleared only by the path that set it is not a guard against every other path; every operation now disarms the retirement confirmation first."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_assertnosiblingoverlap", "label": "AssertNoSiblingOverlap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Visible, enabled, non-zero size was true of two controls printed over each other; the test now fails whenever visible sibling bounds intersect."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_visible_and_bounds_click_assertion", "label": "Visible and Bounds Click Assertion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A synthetic Button.ClickEvent reaches a hidden control exactly as happily as a visible one, so every click asserts IsVisible and non-zero Bounds first."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_projectmembership", "label": "ProjectMembership", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_adr_0158_reference_diagram", "label": "ADR-0158 Reference Diagram", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_ipermissionevaluator_adr_0044", "label": "IPermissionEvaluator ADR-0044", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/50-the-engineering-calculation-workspace.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_50_the_engineering_calculation_workspace_bracketcalculationworkbench_addmaterialasync", "label": "BracketC